      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the core architecture itself is the issue, then the problem isn't a single broken part, but the fundamental design of the system you're using. When you're stuck in a loop of failure, it's often a sign that the software is too deeply intertwined with the flawed hardware to be salvaged. In this scenario, the only true resolution is to cease trying to fix the flawed system and look at completely replacing it.",
      "source": "target",
